Subject: Sample self time per function and per instruction

What this does
  A 1 ms wall-clock tick, driven from the dispatched-op hook, attributes the
  interval since the last tick to the instruction that was running through it.
  Each function's total is written as `us=` on its `F` line and each sampled
  instruction as a `T` line.

Why we need it
  Hotness is by count or by time: a function called a thousand times at ten
  milliseconds is hot, and neither its call count nor its op count says so.

What it adds
  `JSAotProfFunc.sample_us`/`pc_samples`, `js_aot_prof_sample`, the `T` line and
  `us=` in the header line; `profmerge.py` and `profreport.py` carry it.

Needs a bytecode version bump
  No.

